          <msContents>
            <summary>[p]Contents[/p]

[p]1. ff. 1r-13r Bonfacius de Lupis, Founder's Will of the Hospital at Florence, extract[/p]

[p]Title: 'Ordinamenta et instituta egregii militis domini Bonifacii de Lupis, Marchionis Soraniae pro eius hospitale de Florentia'[/p]

[p]Incipit: 'Cum ego Bonifacius de Lupis de Parma Soranie marchio huius hospitalis conditor...'[/p]

[p]Explicit: '...uel omni alio iure quo melius ualere poterint. et hoc per yesum christum dominum nostrum. Amen'.[/p]

[p]There are a few marginal annotations, in Latin and Italian, by various 15th cent. hands. The MS. is a copy of the relevant part of the Founder's Will relating to the Hospital at Florence, which was opened in 1387.[/p]</summary>
            <textLang mainLang="" source="IANA">Latin</textLang>
